<title>SWEDEN: Swedish Riksbank says ERM link not on agenda.</title>
<headline>Swedish Riksbank says ERM link not on agenda.</headline>
<dateline>STOCKHOLM 1996-11-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Urban Backstrom, goveror of Sweden's central bank, the Riksbank, on Thursday reiterated that linking the Swedish crown to Europe's Exchange Rate Mechanism (ERM) was not on the agenda.  </p>
<p>&quot;We are not preparing to join the EMU now. Such a link is not on the agenda,&quot; Backstrom told a public hearing of the state finance committee.</p>
<p>A possible link to the ERM as a precursor to participation in the EMU single currency has been the focus of heated debate in Sweden.</p>
<p>Opinion against taking part in the single currency is strong amongst politicians and Swedes in general, and Backstrom has called for an open debate and better information on the Economic and Monetary Union.</p>
<p>-- Stockholm newsroom +46-8-700 1006</p>
